From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 09:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(terminal): canonical conversation environment identity

Replace the two divergent identity helpers with one canonical
environment_key(task_id, session_id) and migrate every environment-backed
surface to it: terminal, background/PTY processes, process list, file
read/write/patch/search, execute-code (including sandbox RPC dispatch),
environment creation, get_active_env, and cleanup paths (cleanup_vm,
AIAgent.close background-process teardown).

Previously handlers pre-mapped identity through a session-aware helper
while internals re-resolved through a task-only helper, so process list
never matched conversation-scoped spawns and session-close cleanup
silently missed conversation-keyed environments and processes.

The canonical key is opaque (sha256-derived, never embedding the platform
conversation identifier), idempotent for already-derived keys, honors
RL/benchmark isolation overrides in both scopes, and falls back to an
explicit "default" only when no trusted identifier exists.

